#!/bin/sh
# Draw the original artwork or size it to the initial terminal viewport.
art=/usr/share/nodalix/terminal-logo.txt
compact=/usr/share/nodalix/terminal-logo-compact.txt
if [ "$#" -eq 0 ]; then
    exec cat "$art"
fi
if [ "$#" -ne 1 ] || [ "$1" != --welcome ]; then
    printf '%s\n' 'Usage: nodalix-terminal-logo [--welcome]' >&2
    exit 2
fi
if [ "${NODALIX_TERMINAL_LOGO:-1}" = 0 ] || [ "${TERM_PROGRAM:-}" != ghostty ] ||
   [ -n "${SSH_CONNECTION:-}" ] || [ ! -t 0 ] || [ ! -t 1 ]; then
    exit 0
fi

size=$(stty size 2>/dev/null) || exit 0
set -- $size
[ "$#" -eq 2 ] && [ "$1" -gt 2 ] && [ "$2" -gt 1 ] || exit 0
case "${LC_ALL:-${LC_MESSAGES:-${LANG:-C}}}" in
    es|es[_@.]*) spanish=1 ;;
    *) spanish=0 ;;
esac
system_id=$(uname -srm)
disk=$(LC_ALL=C df -k --output=fstype,size,used,pcent / 2>/dev/null)
color=0
[ -n "${NO_COLOR:-}" ] || [ "${TERM:-}" = dumb ] || color=1
LC_ALL=C exec awk -v rows="$(( $1 - 2 ))" -v columns="$(( $2 - 1 ))" \
    -v spanish="$spanish" -v system_id="$system_id" -v disk="$disk" -v color="$color" '
BEGIN {
    escape = sprintf("%c[", 27)
    split("128;155;251 105;164;250 82;175;246 66;187;238 62;201;225 69;212;210 99;222;199", gradient, " ")
}
function styled(code, value) {
    return color ? escape code "m" value escape "0m" : value
}
function detail(label, value) {
    if (value != "")
        details[++detail_count] = sprintf("%-9s %s", label, value)
}
function system_details(    release, version, line, fields, count, elapsed, days, hours, uptime, total, available) {
    release = "/etc/nodalix-release"
    while ((getline line < release) > 0) {
        if (line ~ /^VERSION_ID=/) {
            version = substr(line, 12)
            gsub(/"/, "", version)
            break
        }
    }
    close(release)
    details[++detail_count] = "Nodalix OS" (version ~ /^[0-9][A-Za-z0-9.+-]*$/ ? " " version : "")
    details[++detail_count] = ""
    if (split(system_id, fields, " ") == 3) {
        detail(spanish ? "Sistema" : "System", fields[3])
        detail("Kernel", fields[1] " " fields[2])
    }
    if ((getline line < "/proc/uptime") > 0) {
        elapsed = int(line / 60)
        days = int(elapsed / 1440)
        hours = int(elapsed / 60) % 24
        uptime = (days ? days " d " : "") (hours ? hours " h " : "") (elapsed % 60) " min"
        detail(spanish ? "Actividad" : "Uptime", uptime)
    }
    close("/proc/uptime")
    while ((getline line < "/proc/meminfo") > 0) {
        if (line ~ /^MemTotal:/)
            total = substr(line, 10) + 0
        if (line ~ /^MemAvailable:/) {
            available = substr(line, 14) + 0
            break
        }
    }
    close("/proc/meminfo")
    if (total > 0 && available > 0 && available <= total)
        detail(spanish ? "Memoria" : "Memory", sprintf("%.1f/%.1f GiB %.0f%%",
            (total - available) / 1048576, total / 1048576, 100 * (total - available) / total))
    if (split(disk, fields, "\n") == 2) {
        line = fields[2]
        count = split(line, fields, " ")
        if (count == 4 && fields[2] > 0)
            detail(spanish ? "Disco" : "Disk", sprintf("%.0f/%.0f GiB %s %s",
                fields[3] / 1048576, fields[2] / 1048576, fields[4], fields[1]))
    }
}
function display_detail(row, limit,    value) {
    value = substr(details[row], 1, limit)
    if (!color)
        return value
    if (row == 1)
        return styled("1;38;2;107;214;226", substr(value, 1, 10)) styled("2", substr(value, 11))
    if (row == 2) {
        gsub(/-/, "─", value)
        return styled("38;2;83;135;169", value)
    }
    return styled("2", substr(value, 1, 10)) substr(value, 11)
}
function art_line(edition, row, height, width,    source, column, character, line) {
    source = artwork[edition, int((row + 0.5) * artwork_rows[edition] / height) + 1]
    if (width == artwork_columns[edition])
        return source
    for (column = 0; column < width; column++) {
        character = substr(source, int((column + 0.5) * artwork_columns[edition] / width) + 1, 1)
        line = line (character == "" ? " " : character)
    }
    sub(/ +$/, "", line)
    return line
}
{
    edition = FILENAME == ARGV[1] ? 1 : 2
    artwork[edition, FNR] = $0
    artwork_rows[edition] = FNR
    if (length > artwork_columns[edition])
        artwork_columns[edition] = length
}
END {
    system_details()
    for (row = 1; row <= detail_count; row++)
        if (length(details[row]) > detail_width)
            detail_width = length(details[row])
    details[2] = sprintf("%*s", detail_width, "")
    gsub(/ /, "-", details[2])
    gap = 4
    edition = artwork_rows[1] <= rows && artwork_columns[1] + gap + detail_width <= columns ? 1 : 2
    original_height = artwork_rows[edition]
    original_width = artwork_columns[edition]
    side = original_width + gap + detail_width <= columns && detail_count <= rows
    art_rows = side ? rows : rows - detail_count - 1
    scale = 1
    if (art_rows / original_height < scale)
        scale = art_rows / original_height
    if (columns / original_width < scale)
        scale = columns / original_width
    height = int(original_height * scale)
    width = int(original_width * scale)
    if (height >= 5 && width >= 10 && (!side || height >= detail_count)) {
        top = int((height - detail_count) / 2)
        for (row = 0; row < height; row++) {
            line = art_line(edition, row, height, width)
            hue = "38;2;" gradient[int(7 * row / height) + 1]
            index_in_details = row - top + 1
            if (side && index_in_details in details)
                printf "%s%*s%s\n", styled(hue, line), width - length(line) + gap, "", display_detail(index_in_details, detail_width)
            else
                print styled(hue, line)
        }
        if (side)
            exit
        print ""
    }
    for (row = 1; row <= detail_count && row <= rows; row++)
        print display_detail(row, columns)
}' "$art" "$compact"
